<title>POLAND: GEC-ALSTHOM BUYS POLISH KONSTAL.</title>
<headline>GEC-ALSTHOM BUYS POLISH KONSTAL.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-03-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>French-British consortium Gec-Alsthom has bought a 60-percent stake in Polish rolling stock producer Konstal from 15 Polish National Investment Funds (NFIs), the firm managing NFI 10 said in a statement.</p>
<p>Fidea Management Sp z oo said that GEC-Alsthom bought 33 percent of shares in Konstal from NFI 10 and 27 percent from other 14 NFIs, but did not disclose the value of the transaction.</p>
<p>The state treasury holds a 25 percent stake in Konstal and employees have 15 percent.</p>
<p>The statement said Konstal planned to issue new shares to be taken by Gec-Alsthom, but did not give details.</p>
<p>Konstal, based in Chorzow, south-western Poland, had a net loss of 3.2 million zlotys in the first six months of 1996.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
</text>
